39:  addClue(7.5,6.8,'The address','A page torn from your father’s notebook. The ink is still damp.','Your father wrote “Mara Venn. Ask what came back from the lake.” The date beside it is tomorrow.','notebook');
40:  addClue(14.5,7.8,'A receipt from Bellweather','The last item on the list is a single candle.','The purchase was made three days after the store closed for good. A second receipt is pinned beneath it, same handwriting: yours.','receipt');
41:  addClue(6.6,14.4,'Incident report 114','A typed report from the night the river rose.','Four residents reported missing. The report lists five names. The fifth is blacked out from the inside of the paper.','report');
42:  addClue(22.7,6.8,'Class photograph','A school photograph with one face scratched away.','The empty space is exactly your height. Someone wrote “We kept your desk” on the back.','photograph');
43:  addClue(30.7,7.3,'Ward 3B','A clinical note, folded into the shape of a little house.','“Patient denies having a daughter. Patient asks every hour when she will come home.” The signature is your father’s.','medical');
44:  addClue(15.4,14.4,'The drowned bell','A strip of hymn paper, swollen with river water.','There is a verse here that was never printed: “The town has no dead, only the ones it cannot remember.”','hymn');
45:  addClue(30.8,14.6,'Shift ledger','A factory ledger with the night shift crossed out.','Every worker signed in on the same date, in the same hand. Their final entry reads: “Still hearing it under the floor.”','ledger');
46:  addClue(14.3,30.5,'The sealed tape','An unlabelled microcassette, warm to the touch.','A voice on the tape says your name, then your father says: “If you hear this, don’t let Mara open the door.”','tape');
47:  addClue(23.4,22.7,'Grave 0','A fresh patch of earth with a blank headstone.','The earth is warm. The stone reflects a name that disappears when you turn around.','grave');
48:  addClue(30.7,30.8,'Relay log','A radio log marked with today’s date.','The signal is coming from beneath Ashgate. The operator’s final words: “There is no beneath. There is only the other side.”','relay');
